n-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Bendinelli</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Matteucci</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Desiderio</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>HGF induces CXCR4 and CXCL12-mediated tumor invasion through Ets1 and NF-<italic>&#x003ba;</italic>B</article-title><source><italic>Carcinogenesis</italic></source><year>2007</year><volume>28</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>267</fpage><lpage>279</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16840440</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kukreja</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Abdel-Mageed</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Mondal</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Agrawal</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Up-regulation of CXCR4 expression in PC-3 cells by stromal-derived factor-1<italic>&#x003b1;</italic> (CXCL12) increases endothelial adhesion and transendothelial migration: role of MEK/ERK signaling pathway-dependent NF-<italic>&#x003ba;</italic>B activation</article-title><source><italic>Cancer Research</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>65</volume><issue>21</issue><fpage>9891</fpage><lpage>9898</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16267013</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McClain</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolz</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Davidovich</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Pfannkuch</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Edwards</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bausch</s